#N canvas 20 20 1750 1400 12;
#X text 20 20 g_oled -- the display arbiter \, and the sole owner of the screen (C-5). Five layers with a priority and a time to live \, home < param < modal < diag < alert: callers push semantics on disp \, and the screen redraws on its own clock with whichever layer wins. ref/module/display.md, f 58;
#X text 20 130 creation args: none. inlets: none. outlets: none., f 58;
#X text 20 265 Layers are state \, not draw calls: the next frame draws the last value written \, so a flood and a trickle both come out at ten frames a second and nothing needs rate-limiting., f 58;
#N canvas 30 30 1900 800 disp-in 0;
#X text 20 20 The reserved selectors are this route box: out-l \, out-r and status feed home \, and modal \, modal-off \, diag and alert name a layer. Everything else falls out of the reject and is a parameter., f 58;
#X text 20 115 Callers never name a layer (C-5). A mistyped disp name draws as a nonsense parameter rather than vanishing., f 58;
#X obj 20 250 r disp;
#X obj 20 300 route out-l out-r status modal modal-off alert led grid diag;
#N canvas 40 40 1000 620 levels 0;
#X text 20 20 Derived once per level \, not per frame: the bar width in pixels and the 8px readout \, named out-l and out-r for what u_level reads \, the output (ref/module/audio.md). env~'s 0-100 over 128 px is a scale of 1.28 px per dB., f 58;
