#X text 20 580 This draws to screen 3 \, the buffer already on show \, rather than the ALERT buffer plan-v04.md suggested. There is nothing underneath to preserve: the frame is cleared and rebuilt from stored state ten times a second \, so when the TTL expires the next frame is the meters again. Buffer 4 has SINCE been proven writable and switchable \, and is deliberately still not used: switching is edge-triggered where every layer here is state-driven \, so a lost setscreen would strand the display. See ref/module/display.md., f 58;
