#X text 20 850 The spigot is the cold-start guard: a line with no words would send gPrintln with no typetag \, which packOSC reads as garbage. The count comes from the whole list \, which always exists., f 46;
#X text 420 850 t l l l: count the words \, stash them \, then let the head collect them. C-3, f 46;
#X text 820 850 clip 0 4 caps the text at four words where the typetag is chosen \, so the two cannot disagree. list split 4 truncates to match \, from both its left and its too-short outlet., f 46;
#X text 1220 850 So: sendtyped /oled/gPrintln iiiiiss 3 2 12 24 1 43 % -- five ints \, then a tag per word. packOSC drops a mismatch with an error you cannot see., f 46;
