#X text 1000 360 Right to left: the frame number \, then the name \, which picks the row and whether to write \, then the value \, which commits the line., f 40;
#X text 1000 620 One moses decides update or append: text search returns a known name's row or -1 \, and a miss becomes text size \, which appends., f 40;
#X text 1000 1000 The sixth control is refused until a row ages out \, so nothing shifts while you read it., f 40;
#X text 20 2120 13 frames \, not 12: the layer flag clears on a 1200 ms delay \, so the store outlives it by a frame \, or the layer could win with nothing to draw., f 46;
#X text 620 2120 Aging scans every line from the last toward 0 \, since deleting shifts everything below. until's count bounds the loop., f 40;
